# UI quality bar (Ekum)

## 0. Simplicity first (product philosophy)

Ekum is for busy textile traders. **Clutter-free, fewer taps, never get lost.**

- **One job per screen.** Create/edit/browse/decide — don’t stack CMS controls on an album.
- **Decisions at the moment they matter.** Who / rates / schedule belong on **Publish**, not on every draft edit scroll.
- **Library pickers and long lists open as sheets**, not endless inline grids under the form.
- **No accidental destructive taps.** Remove via explicit ×; tap means view/edit only when we add that later.
- **Challenge feature creep.** Prefer cutting a control over adding a “helpful” second path. If two ways exist, keep the shorter one.
- **Success metric:** a first-time seller can create and publish a pack without hunting menus or re-learning the app.

Before calling UI/product work done, check all four:

## 1. Real estate is not wasted

- Everyday screens: prefer **one tight chrome row**, then content. No stacked pill rows for rare modes.
- Occasional lists (Samples, Returns) belong in **⋯ / You**, not peer tabs next to daily work.
- Section titles only when the **job changes**; drop ranking jargon and redundant subtitles.
- Fake search bars that navigate to empty “type something” voids are wrong — keep feed until the user types.

## 2. Screen does not flicker

- Do **not** put page-rise / enter animations on a persistent shell that re-runs on local state (filters, chips, search typing). Animate **route changes** only.
- Filter/tab switches: keep prior content visible (`useDeferredValue` / `keepPreviousData`); never flash a full-page loader when cached data exists.
- Avoid layout jump: `scrollbar-gutter: stable`; don’t crowd chips so “Done” (or similar) clips or forces horizontal scrollbar thrash.
- Debounce URL sync while typing; don’t remount animated wrappers on every keystroke.

## 2b. Fixed / sticky chrome must not cut content (Required)

Before calling any screen with a fixed or sticky bar done (select bars, composers, CTAs, sheets above bottom nav):

- **Content clearance:** scrollable body has enough bottom (and top) padding that the last card/row/title is fully readable above the chrome — never sliced mid-text.
- **Account for stacked chrome:** bottom nav + sticky action bar heights must both be cleared (e.g. `bottom-20` bar ⇒ padding ≥ nav + bar + gap).
- **Verify on mobile viewport** with the chrome in its active state (selection > 0, composer open, etc.), not only empty.
- Treat clipped content as a **blocking bug** (BM-07), not polish.

## 3. End-to-end feature completes

- Ship the full path: entry → primary UI → secondary homes (⋯ / You) → list/API wired → empty states that match the job.
- Don’t leave a lonely menu item if a natural companion exists and the API already supports it (e.g. Samples + Returns).
- Deep links and redirects must land in the same continuous surface (no stranded “Search” page).
- Verify the happy path in the running app, not only that types compile.

## 4. UX/UI stays consistent (maximum uniformity)

**Default: match what the product already does.** Reuse kit and sibling-screen patterns before inventing chrome. Same job → same control language across Chats, Explore, Orders, sheets, and pickers.

Reuse before inventing:

- **List chrome:** search + one trailing 46×46 square (`ListSearchRow` / Explore filter / Orders·Chats `+`).
- **Selection:** tappable rows with `border-accent bg-accent/5` + quiet Selected/Add/Return/Skip — **not** native checkboxes (except rare secondary toggles like quote “Can’t supply”). See `ConnectionPicker`, return sheet, HowManyEach thumbs.
- **Design lines:** `h-12 w-12` thumb (or initial) + name + compact qty `TextInput` (HowManyEach, dispatch, return).
- **Sheets / CTAs:** kit `Sheet`, full-width primary `Button`, `Field` + `TextInput`/`TextArea`.
- **Errors:** in-sheet `InlineNotice`; page CTAs → danger toast (`z-[90]`). Never bury errors behind an open sheet.
- **Status:** `StatusPill` + shared `status.ts` labels (use `returnStatusLabel` for returns).
- **Other kit:** `Chip` + `FilterRail`, `PageHeader`, `Card` list rows, `EmptyState` / `LoadingBlock`.

Copy voice: plain trader language, short why-lines, no product jargon.

### 4b. Ask before diverging (Required)

If a screen seems to need a **different** component or interaction than the product pattern above:

1. **Stop** — do not ship a one-off checkbox, pill style, header, empty state, or selection gesture.
2. **Ask the user explicitly**, naming both sides, e.g.  
   “Elsewhere we select with accent-border rows (ConnectionPicker / return sheet). For this screen I’m proposing native checkboxes instead — OK to diverge, or match the product pattern?”
3. Only implement the exception after they confirm.

Treat unasked one-offs as a **blocking design bug**, not polish.

## When in doubt

Non-technical textile wholesalers: **plain words, one job per screen, no chrome that fights the content.** Prefer matching a nearby screen over a clever new pattern. Quantities are usually **dozens/hundreds of pieces** — prefer large, tappable piece counts and “same for all”, not tiny retail-style chips (10/15/20).
